  rectangle """extender N(Base) { … }""\n""language L = N(Arg)""" as DECL #FDE68A
  rectangle "<latex>\mathit{ExtenderExpr}</latex>\nunion <latex>\backslash/</latex> · call · ""empty""\n""semantics"" · ""context""\neight content suffixes" as EE #FDE68A
}

package "L1 — presentation content" #EEF2FF {
  rectangle "**DDL text**  [Branch] — //surface sugar//\n""types { ![i64] as Int }""\nread by ""parse_ddl"", which now yields\na **value**, not a second LanguageDef" as DDL #FEF3C7
  rectangle "**Canonical value**  [Proposed] — //normative//\n""[{ &#34;name&#34;: &#34;Int&#34;, &#34;carrier&#34;: &#34;i64&#34; }]""\nmaps · lists · tuples · strings\n(needs no ""syn"")" as VAL #E0E7FF
}

rectangle "**L2 — the seam**  [Implemented]\n""LanguageDef""\n<latex>\mathcal{F} = \texttt{language\_definition\_fingerprint}</latex>" as LD #DBEAFE

rectangle "backends\nparser · rho-native · Dovetail · emitters" as BE #F8FAFC

DECL --> EE : body
EE --> DDL : ""types { … }""
EE --> VAL : ""types = "" <latex>v</latex>   ★ this FIPS

DDL -[#7C3AED,dashed]-> VAL : ""parse_ddl : TokenStream"" <latex>\rightharpoonup</latex> ""Value""\n**desugaring, not a second decoder**\n★ obligation: <latex>\mathcal{E} \circ \mathrm{parse\_ddl} = [\![\,\texttt{DDL} \rightarrow \texttt{LanguageDef}\,]\!]</latex>\n//a stated domain; an ERROR outside it — never a\npartial value// (RT4, §III.2)
VAL --> LD : <latex>\mathcal{E}</latex> — the **sole** decoder
LD --> BE

note bottom of VAL #ECFDF5
  **One decoder FROM A VALUE.** Because ""parse_ddl"" emits a //value// and <latex>\mathcal{E}</latex> is
  the only function from a value to a ""LanguageDef"", the DDL surface cannot drift
  against the value surface: there is no second elaborator between them, no second
  validator, and no second fingerprint. This is the standing //no dual runtime paths//
  discipline applied to the specification frontend.

  ★ **The qualification is not decorative.** ""language!"" still parses Rust tokens
  //directly// into a ""LanguageDef"" (figure 1), because routing it through the value
  form would require every construct to have a v1 value spelling — and gaps G-1 … G-3
  say **two** shipped languages do not: ""RhoCalc"" (G-1, G-3) and ""CalcLambda"" (G-2).
  That arrow is **frozen**, not removed, and the residual drift risk is bounded by
  §VI.3's corpus fingerprint test.

  Only the value form can be **sent on a channel**, **stored in the tuplespace**,
  **versioned in the registry**, **transformed by Rholang code**, and
  **matched with Rholang patterns** — which is why it, and not the text,
  is normative for identity and interchange.
end note

